        "What: The experimental micro-VM runtime, with illustrative request flows. The agent holds no credentials and shares only workspace and tool-cache files with the host over virtiofs. Everything needing a key stays on the host: the MCP gateway, the GitHub MCP server, an API proxy that injects the model key, and the egress firewall.\nWhy: A prompt-injected agent finds no secrets inside the sandbox to steal.\nWhen: Choose it only if you accept experimental status. The boundary covers the agent, not the whole workflow: custom steps or jobs outside the sandbox can still hold secrets.",
